    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i mean i get the compassion part, but doesn't retributive justice serve a purpose by providing justice for victims and holding people truly accountable for their actions? it feels like restorative stuff can sometimes just let people off easy. why do you think the retributive view is less \"morally sound\" in this context?",
